#Archetype: universal character type / plot pattern / setting, common across cultures and history, shared human experience

=Character archetypes

--narrative role (Campbell)
The Hero: undergoes trials (Odysseus, Heracles, Perseus, Theseus)
The Shadow: opposes hero, creates conflict (Hades, Hera, Poseidon)
The Mentor: guides hero (Athena, Chiron)
The Ally: supports hero (Ariadne, Pegasus)
The Herald: brings call to adventure (Hermes, Oracle)
The Guardian: tests hero's resolve (Cerberus, Hydra, Sphinx)
The Shapeshifter: unclear loyalty (Calypso, Circe)
The Trickster: makes mischief (Prometheus, Loki)

=dramatic role (Dramatica)
--major
Protagonist: pursues goal (Harry)
Antagonist: opposes goal (Voldemort)
Guardian: helps towards goal (Dumbledore)
Contagonist: distracts from goal (Snape)
--minor
Sidekick: loyal supporter (Hagrid)
Skeptic: doubts / disbelieves (Draco)
Emotion: acts on feeling (Ron)
Reason: acts on logic (Hermione)

--folktale role (Propp)
Hero: suffers and opposes villain (Snow White, Cinderella)
Villain: causes harm (Evil Queen, Stepmother)
Donor: tests and rewards hero (Huntsman, Fairy Godmother)
Helper: assists hero (Seven Dwarfs, animals)
Prize: provides goal (Prince)
False hero: sabotages hero (Stepsisters)
Dispatcher: sends hero on journey (royal ball)

--Jung's 12 archetypes
The Hero: desires to prove worth, faces danger (Aragorn)
The Caregiver: desires to help and protect (Samwise)
The Explorer: desires to discover (Legolas, Gimli)
The Sage: desires knowledge (Gandalf)
The Magician: desires to understand and change world (Saruman)
The Rebel: desires radical change of system (Gollum)
The Lover: desires intimacy, fears being alone (Arwen)
The Creator: desires to make something of lasting value (Rings of power)
The Jester: desires to bring joy (Pippin)
The Ruler: desires control and power (Sauron)
The Innocent: desires safety and happiness, fears punishment and loss (Frodo)
The Everyman: desires to belong, fears rejection (hobbits)

The Miser: hoards money (Scrooge McDuck)
The Snob: feels superior (Gladstone Gander)
The Fanatic: obsessive devotion (Magica De Spell)
The Fool: bad luck (Donald Duck)
Ineffective Villain: incompetent (Beagle Boys)

